# salesflock environment. Copy to .env (auto-loaded by every binary: `sflock` and each agent's
# runtime — leads, rpa, xeng, lkeng, rdt). Every var here is OPTIONAL — the tools run out of the
# box: Notion and reduck auth come from each tool's own CLI session (keychain), and WHICH store and
# WHICH model an agent uses are its config.ts, never env. Env carries credentials, endpoints and
# ceilings; nothing semantic.

# --- Credentials ---

# Gemini API key (Gemini has no CLI session, so this one key lives here). Needed by any agent whose
# config.ts names a google/* model.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# bedrock models: creds come from the AWS CLI session (SSO) — set only to override your defaults.
# AWS_PROFILE="conception"
# AWS_REGION="us-east-1"          # Bedrock + the us.anthropic.* models live here, not eu-west-3
# aws sso login --profile conception

# Notion: an internal-integration token, INSTEAD of harvesting the `ntn` CLI's session. What the
# review app uses; locally you normally want the keychain session, so leave this unset.
# NOTION_TOKEN=""

# HubSpot private-app token (default: the `hubspot` CLI's OAuth session).
# HUBSPOT_TOKEN=""

# --- The review app ---

# Base URL of the Decisions review app. When set, every decision the runtime prints carries an
# `open` link (`<url>/<decision-id>`) a human clicks to review it. It is ALSO where `sflock docs
# push` sends a revision — so locally point it at the dev server if it isn't on the default port.
# SALESFLOCK_APP_URL="http://localhost:5173"

# Override the "Content to post" data-source id — the documents the app's /write screen edits.
# `sflock docs` pins the id in code (src/docs.ts), like every agent pins its tables, so this is only
# for a fork or a second workspace. Same variable name the app reads.
# NOTION_WRITER_DS=""

# --- Ceilings (one per scarce backend — see src/concurrency.ts for why they differ) ---

# REDUCK_CONCURRENCY="4"     # the browser device: physical
# NOTION_CONCURRENCY="16"    # the Notion API (measured, not the documented 3 rps)
# LLM_CONCURRENCY="8"        # the model provider (Bedrock 429s at 2 on some accounts)
# TASK_CONCURRENCY="8"       # a tool's fan-out over a list

# --- Debugging ---

# Any value ⇒ renderError also prints the root cause's response body and stack.
# DEBUG="1"

# Path to a patched reduck CLI build (default: the bundled @reduck-ai/cli).
# REDUCK_BIN=""